---
{
  "_meta": {
    "io.modelcontextprotocol/serverInfo": {
      "name": "swarmops",
      "title": "SwarmOps",
      "version": "[version]"
    }
  },
  "cacheScope": "public",
  "capabilities": {
    "tools": {}
  },
  "instructions": "SwarmOps is source control for coding-agent swarms: many agents commit to one store at once. Each tool is one store operation, and its result is the SwarmOps envelope {ok, op, api, result | error, meta}, as structuredContent and again as JSON text. A failed operation sets isError and gives error {code, message, retryable, exit, details, hint}: retryable says whether the operation can succeed when it is run again, as it is or after re-reading what the hint names, and a hint is often a swarmops command, whose operation is the tool of the same name (ref list is ref_list, cat read_file, ls read_tree, info repo_info). commit records a changeset and moves no ref. ref_set and ref_delete change a ref by compare-and-swap, so their expected_old is the full 64-hex changeset id the ref held when you read it (from ref_list, show, log or a commit's result). A ref name or a relative revision is read when the call runs instead of pinning the id you read: the ref's own name always matches, so the compare-and-swap protects nothing, and main~1 on ref main never matches; an id prefix stops resolving once another changeset shares it; the server refuses all three. After E_CAS_MISMATCH, commit your change again on top of details.actual, re-applying your edits to the content there, then retry with expected_old set to it. A read may show a commit that a failed sync then takes back; a mutation that names it fails under the lock instead of building on it. Clients limit long tool results and each result carries its envelope twice, so ask for little: max_bytes of 32768 or less for read_file (less for a binary file, which comes back in base64), a limit of 100 or less for read_tree and log, paging on with the cursor a result returns, and max_changes of 100 or less for show. A {\"file\": path} content is read by this server, not by your client: give an absolute path (a relative one, or the server's own stdin or stdout, is refused). Every change is recorded for the agent the server runs as.",
  "resultType": "complete",
  "supportedVersions": [
    "2026-07-28",
    "2025-11-25",
    "2025-06-18"
  ],
  "ttlMs": 3600000
}
